From 8ec48b7f8ea4cb8d80c4b2c7f5c6fa1754b61386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wise <47094117+tjwise99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 02:00:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wpa-supplicant: stop baking credentials

The do_install:append substituted WIFI_SSID and WIFI_PSK_HASH into
/etc/wpa_supplicant.conf at build time. That makes one image serve exactly one
site, and it puts that site's wireless credentials inside every update bundle
built from it. wpa_supplicant reads /data/config/wpa_supplicant.conf instead,
written by provisioning, so the credentials never enter an image or a bundle.

This cannot be expressed as a downstream bbappend: bbappend bodies concatenate,
and there is no mechanism to remove another layer's do_install:append. BBMASK of
the whole bbappend was considered and rejected -- masking it would also revert
upstream's replacement of /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf and change image content.

Upstream submission: suitable -- it is a security fix. Not yet submitted;
upstream has been dormant since 2026-01-20.

Applied by kas at checkout (see includes/base.yaml); the applied tree must equal
the pre-restructure fork content -- verified by diff in the migration PR.
---
 .../wpa-supplicant/wpa-supplicant_%.bbappend         | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meta-autonomos-core/recipes-connectivity/wpa-supplicant/wpa-supplicant_%.bbappend b/meta-autonomos-core/recipes-connectivity/wpa-supplicant/wpa-supplicant_%.bbappend
index da1a90b..1e9ffc3 100644
--- a/meta-autonomos-core/recipes-connectivity/wpa-supplicant/wpa-supplicant_%.bbappend
+++ b/meta-autonomos-core/recipes-connectivity/wpa-supplicant/wpa-supplicant_%.bbappend
@@ -1,7 +1,13 @@
 FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend := "${THISDIR}/${PN}:"
 
-
+# The build-time substitution of WIFI_SSID / WIFI_PSK_HASH is GONE, deliberately.
+# Baking them made one image serve exactly one site and shipped the site's
+# wireless credentials inside every bundle. wpa_supplicant now reads
+# /data/config/wpa_supplicant.conf, which is written by provisioning.
+#
+# The packaged /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf is left as the upstream placeholder with
+# an empty ssid. Nothing reads it any more; it is not removed only because doing
+# so would fight the base recipe's packaging for no benefit.
 do_install:append() {
-    # Replace the empty SSID and password with those provided in WIFI_SSID & WIFI_PSK_HASH
-    sed -i -e s/ssid=\"\"/ssid=\"${WIFI_SSID}\"/ -e s/psk=\"\"/psk=${WIFI_PSK_HASH}/ ${D}/etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
+    :
 }
